---
import stats from '../data/component-analysis.json';
import {modelName} from '../lib/site';
---
<figure class="component-analysis not-prose">
 <div class="bar-legend"><span><i class="room-key"></i>Room-level surface score</span><span><i class="component-key"></i>Component-level surface score</span></div>
 {stats.map(m=><div class="paired-bar-row"><span>{modelName(m)}</span><div><div class="paired-bar room-bar" style={`width:${m.overall/50*100}%`}><b>{m.overall.toFixed(2)}</b></div><div class="paired-bar component-bar" style={`width:${m.component/50*100}%`}><b>{m.component.toFixed(2)}</b></div></div></div>)}
 <figcaption>Paper analysis: seven configurations, 27 matched tasks, and 551 components. Bars share a 0–50 display axis; both normalized metrics range from 0 to 100. Task-level means give each matched task equal weight.</figcaption>
</figure>
